@startuml PresentationLayer
left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false

package "Presentation Layer" {
  class FrontEnd {
    - currentPage: str
    - errorMessage: str
    + viewReviewPage()
    + viewDashboard()
    + approveSituation(id: str)
    + rejectSituation(id: str)
  }

  class APIClient {
    - baseUrl: str
    + getPendingSituations(): list
    + getConfirmedSituations(): list
    + decideSituation(id: str, decision: str)
    + getAnalyticsSummary(): dict
  }
}

FrontEnd --> APIClient : sends requests
note right of FrontEnd
React/Vite user interface.
Provides reviewer and dashboard
screens.
end note
@enduml

@startuml OrchestrationLayer
left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false

package "Orchestration Layer" {
  class FastAPIApp {
    + registerRouters()
    + health(): dict
  }

  class IngestionRouter {
    + health(): dict
    + ingest(event: RawEvent): IngestResponse
  }

  class ProcessingRouter {
    + health(): dict
    + preprocess(request: PreprocessRequest)
    + analyze(request: AnalyzeRequest)
    + runPipeline(request: PipelineRequest)
  }

  class SituationRouter {
    + listSituations(status: str): list
    + decideSituation(id: str, decision: str)
    + analyticsSummary(): dict
  }
}

FastAPIApp o-- IngestionRouter : registers
FastAPIApp o-- ProcessingRouter : registers
FastAPIApp o-- SituationRouter : registers

note right of FastAPIApp
One FastAPI process contains
all routers. The application
is a modular monolith.
end note
@enduml

@startuml InputProcessingModule
left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false

package "Input Processing Module" {
  class DataSimulator <<external tool>> {
    - datasetPath: str
    - interval: float
    + streamPosts()
  }

  class IngestionService {
    + ingest(event: RawEvent): IngestResponse
    + validate(event: RawEvent): bool
    + enrichMetadata(event: RawEvent): dict
  }

  class QueueManager {
    - maxSize: int
    - queue: deque
    + enqueue(item: QueueItem): EnqueueResponse
    + dequeue(): QueueItem
    + dropOldest()
    + stats(): dict
  }

  class RawEvent {
    + text: str
    + createdAt: float
    + attributes: dict
  }

  class IngestedEvent {
    + id: str
    + text: str
    + createdAt: float
    + ingestedAt: float
    + metadata: dict
  }

  class QueueItem {
    + id: str
    + payload: dict
    + enqueuedAt: float
  }

  class Preprocessor {
    + cleanText(text: str): str
    + validate(text: str): bool
    + registerRepost(text: str): int
    + preprocess(text: str): PreprocessResult
  }

  class PreprocessResult {
    + text: str
    + isValid: bool
    + repostCount: int
    + dropped: bool
    + language: LanguageInfo
  }

  class LanguageDetector {
    + detect(text: str): LanguageInfo
    + detectByScript(text: str): str
    + checkCodeMixed(text: str): bool
  }

  class LanguageInfo {
    + lang: str
    + isRomanized: bool
    + isCodeMixed: bool
  }
}

DataSimulator ..> IngestionService : sends posts
IngestionService --> RawEvent : accepts
IngestionService --> IngestedEvent : creates
IngestionService --> QueueManager : enqueues
QueueManager o-- "0..*" QueueItem
QueueItem --> IngestedEvent : contains payload
QueueManager --> Preprocessor : supplies item
Preprocessor --> PreprocessResult : returns
Preprocessor --> LanguageDetector
LanguageDetector --> LanguageInfo

note right of QueueManager
The current implementation
uses an in-memory FIFO deque.
When full, the oldest item
is removed.
end note
@enduml

@startuml AnalysisModule
left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false

package "Analysis Module" {
  abstract class Model {
    + predict(text: str): dict
  }

  class DisasterClassifier {
    + isDisaster: bool
    + confidence: float
    + predict(text: str): dict
  }

  class NeedDetector {
    - thresholds: dict
    + departmentScores: dict
    + predict(text: str): dict
    + activeNeeds(scores: dict): list
    + zeroShotFallback(text: str): dict
  }

  class SentimentAnalyzer {
    + label: str
    + confidence: float
    + negativity: float
    + predict(text: str): dict
    + predictBatch(texts: list): list
  }

  class AnalysisEngine {
    + analyze(text: str): AnalysisResult
    + runPipeline(post: ProcessedPost): AnalysisResult
  }

  class Combiner {
    + computeSeverity(sentiment: dict, needs: dict): float
    + computeActionability(text: str): float
    + combine(results: dict): AnalysisResult
  }

  class AnalysisResult {
    + tweetId: str
    + text: str
    + lang: str
    + isDisaster: bool
    + disasterConfidence: float
    + needs: dict
    + sentiment: dict
    + severity: float
    + actionability: float
    + embedding: list
  }

  class ProcessedPost {
    + tweetId: str
    + text: str
    + createdAt: float
    + lang: str
  }
}

Model <|-- DisasterClassifier
Model <|-- NeedDetector
Model <|-- SentimentAnalyzer

AnalysisEngine --> DisasterClassifier
AnalysisEngine --> NeedDetector
AnalysisEngine --> SentimentAnalyzer
AnalysisEngine --> Combiner
AnalysisEngine --> AnalysisResult : creates
Combiner ..> DisasterClassifier : combines output
Combiner ..> NeedDetector : combines output
Combiner ..> SentimentAnalyzer : combines output
ProcessedPost --> AnalysisEngine

note right of AnalysisEngine
Coordinates disaster,
need, sentiment, and
combined scoring operations.
end note
@enduml

@startuml ClusteringModule
left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false

package "Clustering Module" {
  class EmbeddingGenerator {
    + generate(text: str): list
  }

  class ClusterManager {
    - similarityThreshold: float = 0.32
    - departmentOverlap: float = 0.3
    - timeWindowHours: float = 48
    - minClusterSize: int = 3
    - clusters: list
    + assignPost(result: AnalysisResult): Cluster
    + periodicRecluster(): int
    + getSituations(): tuple
    + clear()
  }

  class Cluster {
    + clusterId: str
    + members: list
    + embeddings: list
    + centroid: list
    + createdAt: datetime
    + updatedAt: datetime
    + departmentRelevance: dict
    + addPost(result: AnalysisResult)
    + size(): int
  }
}

ClusterManager --> EmbeddingGenerator : requests vector
ClusterManager o-- "0..*" Cluster : manages
Cluster o-- "1..*" AnalysisResult : contains
ClusterManager ..> AnalysisResult : assigns

note right of ClusterManager
Posts are grouped using
embedding similarity, time
window, and department overlap.
HDBSCAN can merge clusters
during periodic reclustering.
end note
@enduml

@startuml SituationModule
left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false

package "Situation Module" {
  class SituationManager {
    + createSituation(cluster: Cluster): Situation
    + listSituations(status: str): list
    + approve(id: str): Situation
    + reject(id: str): Situation
    + updateStatus(id: str, status: str)
  }

  class Situation {
    + id: str
    + text: str
    + language: str
    + needs: dict
    + sentiment: dict
    + fakeScore: float
    + priority: dict
    + department: str
    + summary: str
    + evidence: list
    + status: str
    + createdAt: float
  }

  class Summarizer {
    + summarize(cluster: Cluster): str
  }

  enum SituationStatus {
    Pending
    Confirmed
    Rejected
    Routed
    Acknowledged
    Resolved
  }
}

SituationManager o-- "0..*" Situation
SituationManager --> Cluster : receives
SituationManager --> Summarizer
Situation --> SituationStatus

note right of SituationStatus
Pending, Confirmed, and
Rejected are currently used.
Routed, Acknowledged, and
Resolved are planned.
end note

note right of Summarizer
The endpoint currently
returns a shortened text
result. Full model-based
summarization is planned.
end note
@enduml

@startuml EvidenceModule
left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false

package "Evidence Module" {
  class EvidenceManager {
    + extract(cluster: Cluster, topK: int): list
    + topPosts(cluster: Cluster): list
    + store(evidence: Evidence)
  }

  class Evidence {
    + id: str
    + postId: str
    + clusterId: str
    + text: str
    + metadata: dict
  }

  class PrivacyManager {
    + maskPersonalDetails(text: str): str
    + maskMetadata(metadata: dict): dict
  }

  class EvidenceRanker {
    + rank(posts: list): list
    + selectRepresentativePosts(posts: list, topK: int): list
  }
}

EvidenceManager --> EvidenceRanker : selects posts
EvidenceManager --> PrivacyManager : protects data
EvidenceManager o-- "0..*" Evidence : manages
EvidenceManager --> Cluster : reads members

note right of PrivacyManager
Masks phone numbers and
sensitive metadata before
evidence is stored.
end note
@enduml

@startuml PersistentModule
left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false

package "Persistent Module" {
  class DatabaseClient {
    - uri: str
    - databaseName: str
    + getCollection(name: str)
    + save(collection: str, document: dict): str
    + find(collection: str, query: dict): list
    + findOne(collection: str, query: dict): dict
    + update(collection: str, query: dict, values: dict): bool
    + delete(collection: str, query: dict): bool
  }

  class MongoDB {
    + situations
    + evidence
  }

  class Situation
  class Evidence
}

DatabaseClient --> MongoDB : uses Motor client
MongoDB o-- Situation : stores
MongoDB o-- Evidence : stores

note right of DatabaseClient
The current implementation
is in backend/app/db.py.
It provides shared asynchronous
MongoDB helper functions.
end note
@enduml

@startuml ReviewRoutingModule
left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false

package "Review and Routing Module" {
  class ReviewService {
    + approve(situation: Situation)
    + reject(situation: Situation)
    + castVote(situation: Situation, vote: ReviewVote)
    + autoDemote(situation: Situation)
  }

  class ReviewVote {
    + reviewerId: str
    + vote: str
    + timestamp: datetime
  }

  class RoutingService {
    - queueMultiplier: dict
    + route(situation: Situation)
  }

  class DepartmentQueue {
    + department: str
    + situations: list
    + addSituation(situation: Situation)
    + updateStatus(id: str, status: str)
  }

  class Situation
}

ReviewService --> Situation
ReviewService o-- "0..*" ReviewVote
ReviewService --> RoutingService : after approval
RoutingService --> DepartmentQueue
DepartmentQueue o-- "0..*" Situation

note right of ReviewService
Approve and reject are
partially implemented.
True/fake voting and
automatic demotion are planned.
end note

note right of RoutingService
Department queues and
the officer lifecycle are
planned functionality.
end note
@enduml